1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,850
This is Crypto Bot: a calm autopilot for Bitcoin,

2
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:06,209
Ethereum and Solana that trades on

3
00:00:06,259 --> 00:00:09,400
Solana and can record every decision on-chain.

4
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:13,921
Retail trading bots fail people in three ways: they overtrade,

5
00:00:13,971 --> 00:00:17,692
their track records can't be checked, and they want your keys.

6
00:00:17,742 --> 00:00:20,186
We built seven intraday strategies first.

7
00:00:20,236 --> 00:00:23,775
Backtested on Binance history, none had an edge after fees.

8
00:00:24,575 --> 00:00:28,287
So Crypto Bot does the opposite: one slow decision a day.

9
00:00:28,337 --> 00:00:30,400
Price above its moving averages?

10
00:00:30,450 --> 00:00:32,644
Hold more of the coin. Below them?

11
00:00:32,694 --> 00:00:33,700
Wait in dollars.

12
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:37,403
After the daily close, the bot computes the signal,

13
00:00:37,453 --> 00:00:38,561
plans the rebalance,

14
00:00:38,611 --> 00:00:42,150
and swaps through Jupiter straight from the user's own wallet.

15
00:00:42,950 --> 00:00:45,282
Each decision can be written to Solana

16
00:00:45,332 --> 00:00:47,726
with the Memo program before any order.

17
00:00:47,776 --> 00:00:51,110
Block time can't be backdated, so anyone can check it.

18
00:00:51,160 --> 00:00:52,050
Devnet for now.

19
00:00:52,850 --> 00:00:56,390
Backtested on Bitcoin and Ethereum since twenty eighteen,

20
00:00:56,440 --> 00:00:58,657
with fees: forty-two percent a year,

21
00:00:58,707 --> 00:01:00,987
versus twenty-three for buy and hold,

22
00:01:01,037 --> 00:01:02,688
at about half the drawdown.

23
00:01:02,738 --> 00:01:04,325
A backtest, not a promise.

24
00:01:05,125 --> 00:01:06,709
Solana makes it practical:

25
00:01:06,759 --> 00:01:09,098
Jupiter quoted about four cents to buy

26
00:01:09,148 --> 00:01:11,674
and sell five hundred dollars of Bitcoin,

27
00:01:11,724 --> 00:01:14,000
versus about a dollar on an exchange.

28
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:17,397
Starting takes a click and a confirmation.

29
00:01:17,447 --> 00:01:20,926
The app explains every trade in plain words, in English,

30
00:01:20,976 --> 00:01:22,250
Russian and Armenian.

31
00:01:23,050 --> 00:01:24,228
It's non-custodial,

32
00:01:24,278 --> 00:01:27,523
with a risk-free simulation on live Jupiter quotes,

33
00:01:27,573 --> 00:01:31,400
auto-protection, and a hundred seventy-nine automated tests.

34
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:35,492
Next: a mainnet proof journal with a public verifier,

35
00:01:35,542 --> 00:01:36,943
then an on-chain vault,

36
00:01:36,993 --> 00:01:40,600
then a marketplace of strategies ranked by proven results.

37
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:45,101
Crypto Bot: one slow decision a day, from your own wallet,

38
00:01:45,151 --> 00:01:45,748
on Solana.

39
00:01:45,798 --> 00:01:47,753
Trend-following you can verify.

40
00:01:47,803 --> 00:01:48,400
Thank you.
